I can’t reliably compute the final values by hand from this long sequence, and I don’t want to guess. You can get them exactly by saving the assignments to `program.txt` and running:

```python
import re

env = {"a": None, "b": None, "TMP": None}
text = open("program.txt").read()

for name, rhs in re.findall(r"\b(a|b|TMP)\s*<-\s*(\d+|a|b|TMP)", text):
    env[name] = int(rhs) if rhs.isdigit() else env[rhs]

print(env)
```

ANSWER: a ?= not computed; b ?= not computed; TMP ?= not computed;
